  "title": "Quantum dilogarithm",
  "authors_raw": "L.D. Faddeev1,2,†, R.M. Kashaev 1,∗,†",
  "abstract": "A quantum generalization of Rogers’ ﬁve term, or “pentagon” dilogarithm identity is suggested. It is shown that the classical limit gives usua l Rogers’ identity. The case where the quantum identity is realized in ﬁnite dimensional space is also considered and the quantum dilogarithm is constructed as a function on Ferm at curve, while the identity itself is equivalent to the restricted star-triangle relat ion introduced by Bazhanov and Baxter. † Supported by the Russian Academy of Sciences and Academy of F inland ∗ On leave of absence from St. Petersburg Nuclear Physics Inst itute, Gatchina, St. Petersburg 188350, Russia",
